  "worked_solution": "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m\u2220A={30}^{\u2218}.$ Notice that relative to $\u2220A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{\u2015}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(m\u2220A) & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061({30}^{\u2218}) & =\\frac{x-1}{x+2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061({30}^{\u2218})(x+2) & =x-1 \\\\ x\\operatorname{tan}\u2061({30}^{\u2218})+2\\operatorname{tan}\u2061({30}^{\u2218}) & =x-1 \\\\ x\\operatorname{tan}\u2061({30}^{\u2218})-x & =-1-2\\operatorname{tan}\u2061({30}^{\u2218}) \\\\ x(\\operatorname{tan}\u2061({30}^{\u2218})-1) & =-1-2\\operatorname{tan}\u2061({30}^{\u2218}) \\\\ x(1-\\operatorname{tan}\u2061({30}^{\u2218})) & =1+2\\operatorname{tan}\u2061({30}^{\u2218}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1+2\\operatorname{tan}\u2061({30}^{\u2218})}{1-\\operatorname{tan}\u2061({30}^{\u2218})} \\\\ x & =5.098\\,0\u2026\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =x-1=5.098\\,0-1=4.098\\,0\u2026, \\\\ AB & =x+2=5.098\\,0+2=7.098\\,0\u2026.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $\u25b3ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}(4.098\\,0\u2026)(7.098\\,0\u2026) \\\\  & =14.543\\,8\u2026 \\\\  & \u224814.5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the one decimal place.",
